From 1220ccfe884df2a82f5bbda7d46c9667998525ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: will <will-tm@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 15:22:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 01/20] hw/arm: add i.MX6SX SoC container header

Address map and IRQ numbers for the Nest Display-3.4 board (i.MX6SX),
taken from the board's own stock Device Tree rather than the i.MX6Q
map: UART2-5 sit on AIPS2, a third bus lives at 0x02200000, the
GPMI/BCH/APBH block at 0x0180xxxx, and there is no PCIe.
---
 include/hw/arm/fsl-imx6sx.h | 250 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 250 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 include/hw/arm/fsl-imx6sx.h

diff --git a/include/hw/arm/fsl-imx6sx.h b/include/hw/arm/fsl-imx6sx.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..3419540
--- /dev/null
+++ b/include/hw/arm/fsl-imx6sx.h
@@ -0,0 +1,250 @@
+/*
+ * i.MX6SX SoC emulation (Nest Display-3.4 / "Flintstone" board)
+ *
+ * Address map and IRQ numbers are taken from the board's own Device Tree
+ * blob (stock firmware `fdt@3`, compatible "nestlabs,diamond3-dvt",
+ * "fsl,imx6sx"), NOT from the i.MX6 Quad map — the 6SX differs in several
+ * places (UART2-5 sit on AIPS2, there is a third AIPS bus at 0x02200000,
+ * the GPMI/BCH/APBH block lives at 0x01800000, and there is no PCIe).
